Subject: [PATCH 2/5] docs(readme): state the app e2e listed counts and the
 measured G0 baseline

apps/desktop listed screens.a11y as 180 cases and omitted the 45 behavioural
cases. The desktop project lists 793: a11y 188, states 252, visual 308, flows 30,
layout 12, onboarding 3. Record what harness.ts stubs (the Tauri get_config edge
and the RPC surface) against what real-acceptance.cjs proves (the built bundle
on a live warshad with no RPC stub).

The G0 baseline at 0772d50 is now recorded, so explain the 180-vs-188 gap from
the artifact rather than leaving it open: 785 passed / 8 failed, all eight on
the settings screen's a11y case. G0's verdict is fail, not pass.

apps/remote described bench.tsx as layout. It is the data context
(RemoteProvider/useRemote, stageQueue, gateWaitsOnOwner); the UI is the five
screens plus chrome/GatePlate/pairing. Document the build-time dist/sw.js, the
production-only registerShellWorker call, the absence of any push permission,
and the 91 listed remote cases against G0's measured 51 passed / 40 failed.
